{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Rea-Sixty\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER extension that drives the SSL UF8 and UC1 control surfaces natively over their vendor-USB protocol. Replaces SSL 360\u176 ? without requiring an SSL plug-in on every track.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 What it does\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b DAW-layer track colours} on the UF8 scribble strips \u8212- every REAPER track shows its assigned colour, no per-track plug-in needed\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Full 16-bit faders} with motor + touch\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b UC1 follows the focused REAPER track} and drives the SSL Channel Strip 2 / Bus Compressor 2 / 4K B/E/G / 360\u176 ? Link plug-ins\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b UC1 GR meter} driven from the SSL plug-in itself via REAPER's PreSonus VST3 {\f1 GainReduction_dB} host extension\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Generic FX Learn} for any VST/JS/AU plug-in parameter (FX-name substring match \u8212- slot reorders are safe, renames break the binding)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b REC + RME (TotalReaper) integration} \u8212- per-strip preamp mirror (gain / phantom / pad / phase) plus Shift+V-Pot input-channel switch when TotalReaper is detected\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Bindings system} \u8212- modifier combos (incl. double-click latch on Shift), Learn mode, right-click Copy / Paste, per-binding colour overrides\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Settings window} in a dockable ReaImGui context \u8212- seven tabs (Device, Bindings, Modes, FX Learn, Selection Sets, Parameter Groups, About) themed to REAPER's active theme\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 After install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Preferences -> Control/OSC/Web -> Add -> {\b Rea-Sixty}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 First-run setup buttons (Windows WinUSB driver + Linux udev rule) live in Settings -> About; macOS needs no extra setup.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Linux constraint: plug UF8 and UC1 into {\b separate} PC USB ports. Daisy-chaining (UC1 through UF8's downstream port) triggers {\f1 xhci_hcd} port-resets on Linux 6.17.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab REAPER 6 or later\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ReaImGui} (install separately via ReaPack) \u8212- without it the Settings window stays empty, hardware control still works\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab SSL 360\u176 ? {\b not running} (it claims the UF8/UC1 vendor interface exclusively)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Vendor relationship\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Not affiliated with Solid State Logic. SSL ACP Support replied to the project author on 2026-05-18 confirming "no objections to the public, open source-project" but declined to share protocol documentation. Protocol stays self-decoded; firmware-update breakage is on the project to chase.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaMark Comments\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER integration for the ReaMark audio review platform. Load a project by share link, view the waveform with comment markers, and create, reply to, resolve, edit or delete timeline comments directly from REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires the ReaImGui extension (install via ReaPack). Configure your ReaMark server URL and log in inside the script.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TotalReaper\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER \u8596 ? RME TotalMix FX Global OSC bridge. Turns RME interfaces (UFX+ family) into a fully DAW-controlled hardware console \u8212- mic gain, 48V phantom, pad, phase, submix sends, all driven from REAPER tracks via TotalMix FX 2.1's Global OSC protocol.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i In Erinnerung an ASIO Direct Monitoring in Samplitude.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 What it does\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Routing mirror}: REAPER track volume / mute / pan \u8594 ? TotalMix input matrix in real time. REAPER's software monitor is muted while the mirror is engaged so you only hear TotalMix's hardware (zero-latency) path.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b 2-Way Control}: optional reverse direction \u8212- TotalMix fader/balpan moves drive matching REAPER tracks and direct sends. Echo-suppression keeps the loop stable.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Track-to-track sends} are walked recursively and projected onto TotalMix routings on every hardware-output destination \u8212- cue mixes, headphone sends, etc.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Per-track preamp control} as REAPER actions: gain \u177 ?1 dB, 48V toggle, pad toggle (with mute pulse to hide the hardware pop), phase invert, AutoLevel. Multi-select.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Studio actions}: Toggle Talkback, Toggle Auto-Talkback on Stop (drives talkback from REAPER's transport state), Save/Load TotalMix Snapshot Slot 1\u8230 ?8.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Stereo input handling}: optionally link REAPER stereo inputs as TotalMix stereo pairs \u8212- pan/balance and stereo width round-trip both directions; unlinks automatically on stereo\u8594 ?mono. 2-mono splits still work too.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Settings window} (action "TotalReaper: Open Settings Window"): configurable OSC ports (applied live) and feature toggles, kept in sync with the matching actions. Needs ReaImGui.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab REAPER 6 or later (tested through 7.71)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab TotalMix FX 2.1 Alpha 4 or later, with Global OSC enabled (Settings \u8594 ? OSC \u8594 ? Compatibility Mode \u8594 ? Global OSC)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab RME interface that supports Global OSC (UFX+, UCX II, etc.)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaImGui \u8212- only for the optional Settings window; install via ReaPack \u8594 ? Browse packages. Everything else works without it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b TotalMix Settings \u8594 ? OSC \u8594 ? Details\u8230 ? \u8594 ? "Receive to hidden channels" must be checked.} Otherwise TotalMix silently drops fader writes for any input row or output column not in the current layout \u8212- the routing mirror appears dead even though TotalReaper is sending correctly. Some TotalMix versions default this OFF.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Out of scope\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TotalMix-internal effects (channel EQ, dynamics, room EQ, FX send/return) \u8212- those stay in TotalMix.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 After install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Find all actions in REAPER's Action List by typing "TotalReaper". Run {\b TotalReaper: Toggle Routing Mirror} to engage.\par}
}
